  number    =  100228,
  pages     =  100228,
  abstract  = "Introduction: The complement system and neutrophil extracellular
               traps (NETs) might contribute to ischemia-reperfusion injury in
               ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI). We aimed to estimate
               associations between complement activation and NETs in STEMI, and
               their prognostic value on clinical endpoints. Methods: In this
               cohort study, 864 patients admitted for PCI during STEMI were
               included. Complement activation was analyzed by the terminal
               complement complex (TCC), while NETs were analyzed by
               myeloperoxidase-DNA, citrullinated histone 3 (CitH3) and dsDNA.
               The composite endpoint was reinfarction, unscheduled
               revascularization, stroke, hospitalization due to heart failure,
               or death, and the secondary endpoint was total mortality. The
               association between TCC and clinical endpoints was assessed by
