              purine nucleotides needed for cell growth. Science, this issue p.
              728; see also p. 670 Coupling cellular growth signals to synthesis
              of RNA and DNA. [Also see Perspective by Ma and Jones] In response
              to growth signals, mechanistic target of rapamycin complex 1
              (mTORC1) stimulates anabolic processes underlying cell growth. We
              found that mTORC1 increases metabolic flux through the de novo
              purine synthesis pathway in various mouse and human cells, thereby
              influencing the nucleotide pool available for nucleic acid
